1
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,110
I'll never forget those days.

2
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:13,320
First year of middle school,
beginning of summer.

3
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:16,320
On my way home.

4
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:18,910
A passing shower.

5
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,540
Really came out of nowhere, didn't it?

6
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:20,020
Yeah.

7
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
Su

8
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
mm

9
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
er

10
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
Fe

11
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
st

12
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
iv

13
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,420
al

14
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,900
Tanaka-kun, going to the festival?

15
00:02:03,710 --> 00:02:07,610
Wonder if Yumi-chan's going.
I'd better ask her later.

16
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:16,180
Here, use this.

17
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:18,800
Wipe your hair.

18
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:21,820
You'll catch a cold otherwise.

19
00:02:24,250 --> 00:02:26,030
Is this your gym shirt?

20
00:02:26,030 --> 00:02:29,130
Don't worry, it's clean. Never really used it.

21
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,360
Just once.

22
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:34,480
What?! So you have used it!

23
00:02:44,020 --> 00:02:46,680
Fine then! Have it your way.

24
00:02:46,680 --> 00:02:48,730
Yeah, go right ahead.

25
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:50,980
Thanks.

26
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:03,160
Tanaka-kun was in the class next to mine.

27
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:09,880
He was short, and his voice wasn't very deep. Almost like a girl.

28
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,160
Thank you.

29
00:03:13,770 --> 00:03:15,800
Are you going to the summer festival?

30
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,760
Have you already made plans with your friends?

31
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:23,170
Not yet...

32
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:24,470
Seven o'clock.

33
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:30,750
By the clock in Triangle Park.

34
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,320
Hey.

35
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:44,030
What's going on with you and Tanaka? You dating or something?

36
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:46,240
C'mon, spill it!

37
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,330
Just shut your mouth!

38
00:03:48,890 --> 00:03:51,200
This is why I hate boys.

39
00:03:51,990 --> 00:03:53,710
Boys should just...

40
00:03:53,710 --> 00:03:55,470
...all die in a fire!

41
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:15,190
Seven o'clock, by the clock in Triangle Park.

42
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:19,460
The minutes passed by with no sign of Tanaka-kun.

43
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:24,200
Seriously? Tanaka's gone?

44
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:26,940
Yeah, I heard he moved away during summer vacation.

45
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:28,920
Could've at least told me.

46
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:30,670
What, you didn't know either?

47
00:04:32,450 --> 00:04:35,420
He was as awkward as they came,

48
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:36,920
indecisive,

49
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:41,670
and never sure of his place.

50
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:50,240
But I was still in love with Tanaka-kun.

51
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:55,890
Even now, a small part of my heart belongs to him.

52
00:04:58,070 --> 00:04:59,390
Sometimes, I think,

53
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,870
"I want to go back to those days."

54
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:19,000
Three years have passed.

55
00:05:19,710 --> 00:05:22,510
I, Yoshioka Futaba,

56
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:26,720
live a peaceful life...

57
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:32,720
Mom! Why didn't you wake me?!

58
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:36,850
I'm about to start the third semester of my first year of high school.

59
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:56,660
Oh no!

60
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:01,000
Futaba, morning.

61
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,090
Yo! Morning, Chie-chan!

62
00:06:04,090 --> 00:06:06,220
Here. Thanks for lending it to me.

63
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,300
No prob.

64
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:12,760
Girl, you gotta take better care of yourself.

65
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:14,680
You're seriously lacking in allure.

66
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,230
Don't think I don't know any better.

67
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:19,480
This is all on purpose.

68
00:06:20,860 --> 00:06:22,940
You're hopeless, Futaba.

69
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:27,450
But that's what I like about Futaba!

70
00:06:27,450 --> 00:06:29,490
Yo! Morning, Asumi!

71
00:06:29,490 --> 00:06:31,990
You're nothing like that.

72
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,660
Makita, good morning.

73
00:06:35,370 --> 00:06:36,620
Hello.

74
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:41,000
Look at 'em slobbering all over her.

75
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,500
She's not even all that pretty, either.

76
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,840
They just like the idea of her.

77
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:51,970
Makita Yuuri. Is she fine with the way things are?

78
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:56,020
All the girls in class hate and ostracize her.

79
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:57,640
Just looking at her pisses me off.

80
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:58,770
I wouldn't be able to take it.

81
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,810
She acts all cutesy in front of the boys.

82
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:01,980
That was my life the last two years of middle school.

83
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:03,270
Yeah, right? Just because she's a little pretty...

84
00:07:03,270 --> 00:07:04,440
She's the worst.

85
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:05,440
I didn't want to be alone.

86
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:07,440
So I made my decision.

87
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:12,200
With the clean slate I received at high school, I remade myself as a brand-new Futaba!

88
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:16,870
I wanted the girls to like me, so I took all the allure I had and killed it, killed it,

89
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,080
killed it!

90
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:21,540
I'm starving! Let's go eat already!

91
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,040
You sure love stuffing yourself.

92
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,920
You blow my mind every day, Futaba.

93
00:07:28,090 --> 00:07:29,340
Tanaka!

94
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:37,390
Want some gum?

95
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:40,350
Come on, I told you to call me "Sensei"!

96
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:42,810
So you want some or not?

97
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:43,730
Give it.

98
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:48,400
What's this I smell? Love?

99
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:48,990
Huh?!

100
00:07:48,990 --> 00:07:54,410
You're not fooling anyone! You've never shown any interest in guys, and now you're going gaga over Tanaka-sensei!

101
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:56,450
Hey, come on! I don't...

102
00:07:57,030 --> 00:08:01,330
We're just kidding. Love and you mix like oil and water.

103
00:08:02,210 --> 00:08:04,920
Yeah, never in a million years.

104
00:08:07,550 --> 00:08:11,010
Dude, don't you think Yoshioka
from Class 2's kinda cute?

105
00:08:11,010 --> 00:08:12,930
No, stop it!

106
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:15,640
I guess, but isn't she...

107
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:15,720
Bulky Beef Bun

108
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:17,390
Now, behold!

109
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:15,850
Bulky Beef Bun

110
00:08:15,850 --> 00:08:15,970
Bulky Beef Bun

111
00:08:15,970 --> 00:08:16,100
Bulky Beef Bun

112
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:16,390
Bulky Beef Bun

113
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,390
Hey!

114
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,810
The heck are you doing?

115
00:08:20,810 --> 00:08:22,770
Yeah, never mind.

116
00:08:22,770 --> 00:08:24,270
See?

117
00:08:25,230 --> 00:08:27,110
Did you hear those guys?

118
00:08:27,110 --> 00:08:32,320
Futaba, I be you'd be drowning in boys if you cleaned up a bit.

119
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:35,570
Please, like I care about that.

120
00:08:35,570 --> 00:08:37,830
You know I hate guys.

121
00:08:38,410 --> 00:08:41,750
As long as I've got you two, guys can all just—

122
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:52,760
What unflattering bread.

123
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,190
Tanaka-kun?

124
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,570
Futaba, let's go.

125
00:09:12,110 --> 00:09:14,900
There's something I forgot to buy.

126
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:15,950
Huh?

127
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,280
Sorry, I'll be right there.

128
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:26,830
His voice and height are completely different...

129
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,290
I didn't even see his face...

130
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:35,170
Why am I so convinced that he's Tanaka-kun?

131
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:52,690
Mabuchi!

132
00:10:02,370 --> 00:10:04,750
Mabuchi, buying lunch now?

133
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:07,670
"Mabuchi"?

134
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:09,250
I'll tag along.

135
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:20,970
It wasn't him.

136
00:10:24,850 --> 00:10:28,060
Good thing I didn't try to talk to him.

137
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:34,570
Though the fake Tanaka-kun did smirk when our eyes met.

138
00:10:36,110 --> 00:10:40,450
And judging from his blue shoes, he's a first-year like me.

139
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,580
I can't believe myself.

140
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:49,870
Why would I even think he was Tanaka-kun?

141
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:55,050
Ah!

142
00:10:59,430 --> 00:11:03,390
I'm not following you or anything!
We just happen to be going the same way!

143
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,270
I-I messed up.

144
00:11:20,490 --> 00:11:25,780
Really, I'm not following him.
I just happen to live this way.

145
00:11:28,370 --> 00:11:30,540
Huh? Just a minute here...

146
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:34,080
Wait, did he live in the same neighborhood as me?

147
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,350
Really came out of nowhere, didn't it?

148
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:00,530
I knew it...

149
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:04,160
I knew it!

150
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:07,160
I knew it!

151
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:16,960
Ta... Tanaka-kun?

152
00:12:20,710 --> 00:12:22,970
My name's Mabuchi.

153
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,140
Sorry! I thought you were someone else.

154
00:12:34,310 --> 00:12:36,770
Really came out of nowhere, didn't it?

155
00:12:59,340 --> 00:13:01,010
So you are Tanaka-kun!

156
00:13:01,800 --> 00:13:04,090
Well, not anymore.

157
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:06,720
I'm Mabuchi Kou now.

158
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:11,100
After my parents divorced,

159
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,430
my name changed.

160
00:13:15,190 --> 00:13:16,560
His voice, his height,

161
00:13:17,770 --> 00:13:19,900
and even his name have changed.

162
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,150
But still...

163
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:25,700
The person before my eyes right now

164
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:30,910
is the first boy I ever loved.

165
00:13:32,490 --> 00:13:38,250
You didn't realize who I was for two whole semesters.

166
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,300
I knew you'd get it eventually,

167
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,170
but I didn't expect it to take this long.

168
00:13:44,090 --> 00:13:45,340
You're a riot.

169
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:48,680
Is this how these things usually go?

170
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:53,560
I recognized you right away,
even with how you turned out.

171
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,980
What are you implying?!

172
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:58,560
You're certainly not the quiet girl I used to know.

173
00:13:59,060 --> 00:14:03,230
I-If you knew, you should've said something sooner!

174
00:14:03,230 --> 00:14:05,690
And you've changed just as much as me, Tanaka-kun!

175
00:14:05,690 --> 00:14:08,360
I told you, I'm not Tanaka anymore.

176
00:14:08,360 --> 00:14:10,450
My damn name's Mabuchi.

177
00:14:11,120 --> 00:14:14,330
Geez... have I ever met such a scary person?

178
00:14:14,330 --> 00:14:17,160
Not like I'm one to talk...

179
00:14:17,410 --> 00:14:19,580
Well, putting that aside,

180
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:22,040
wanna go for a reunion hug?

181
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,380
Come.

182
00:14:26,920 --> 00:14:29,390
No! Who even thinks of that?!

183
00:14:29,390 --> 00:14:31,260
What do you mean, "come"?!

184
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,060
I almost forgot.

185
00:14:33,060 --> 00:14:37,390
You've always had it out for guys.

186
00:14:38,140 --> 00:14:39,730
I guess that hasn't changed.

187
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:43,440
Boys should just all die in a fire!

188
00:14:47,150 --> 00:14:49,070
Yeah, I hate them.

189
00:14:49,610 --> 00:14:51,200
Always have.

190
00:14:51,950 --> 00:14:52,910
But...

191
00:14:54,870 --> 00:15:00,710
kudarizaka fumikiri made

192
00:14:54,870 --> 00:15:00,710
Before I knew it, I had run

193
00:14:56,580 --> 00:14:59,080
You're an exception.

194
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:02,080
I never got to tell you.

195
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:05,710
atashi wa muchuu de hashitta

196
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:05,710
all the way down to the train tracks.

197
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:11,390
kono koi wo saegiru you ni

198
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:11,390
What I found was a train departing,

199
00:15:08,300 --> 00:15:11,010
So that's... how it was.

200
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:16,270
densha wa sugisatta

201
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:16,270
taking my love with it.

202
00:15:16,010 --> 00:15:17,100
Same here.

203
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:21,940
tooi hi no kioku  umi no kagayaki

204
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:21,940
Distant memories, shining seas.

205
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:23,770
I... really did...

206
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:24,820
kisetsu wa meguru

207
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:24,820
Seasons pass.

208
00:15:24,770 --> 00:15:25,980
...love you.

209
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:29,190
hikoukigumo ni me wo hosomete

210
00:15:24,820 --> 00:15:29,190
Now, I squint up at the clouds.

211
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:34,580
chiisaku yureta himawari

212
00:15:29,190 --> 00:15:34,580
A sunflower swayed in the breeze,

213
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,740
This feels just like those days I've longed for...

214
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:40,960
sayonara mo ienai mata

215
00:15:34,580 --> 00:15:40,960
seeing how I couldn't even say goodbye.

216
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:39,540
I can go back...

217
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:50,800
hon no suumiri no sukima de sotto kusuguru itami

218
00:15:40,960 --> 00:15:50,800
We were so tantalizingly close, yet so far apart.

219
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:52,890
We can never go back.

220
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:56,350
manatsu ni kieta hanabi ga

221
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:56,350
If only the summer fireworks

222
00:15:55,550 --> 00:15:58,020
Things have changed since then.

223
00:15:56,350 --> 00:16:02,270
namida no saki ni utsureba

224
00:15:56,350 --> 00:16:02,270
had appeared before my tears...

225
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:00,180
Both for you and for me.

226
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:05,770
It's all in the past now.

227
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:07,690
I will kitto omoidasu wa

228
00:16:02,270 --> 00:16:07,690
I will definitely remember.

229
00:16:07,690 --> 00:16:19,450
anata ni todoke kono basho de atashi wa matteiru

230
00:16:07,690 --> 00:16:19,450
Please know that I'll be here, waiting for you.

231
00:16:10,190 --> 00:16:14,620
This must be his way of telling me to forget about it.

232
00:16:16,950 --> 00:16:20,040
Come on, don't cry on me now.

233
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:22,960
Stupid.

234
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:24,330
Later.

235
00:16:25,210 --> 00:16:29,090
But even as he spoke such uncaring words,

236
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:33,970
chiisaku yureta himawari

237
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:33,970
A sunflower swayed in the breeze.

238
00:16:29,550 --> 00:16:32,050
I heard a tinge of sadness in his voice.

239
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:40,310
ano hi no mama no atashi wa

240
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:40,310
Back then, I couldn't even

241
00:16:35,930 --> 00:16:37,470
Or at least I think so.

242
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:45,060
nobita maegami mo mitometaku nai

243
00:16:40,310 --> 00:16:45,060
accept seeing my bangs grow.

244
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:48,150
Back then, I didn't know.

245
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:51,990
nani mo kawattenai

246
00:16:45,560 --> 00:16:51,990
I haven't changed at all.

247
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:55,660
I thought that I'd be able to talk it out with Tanaka-kun after summer vacation.

248
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:57,870
kaze no oto ni furikaeru

249
00:16:52,690 --> 00:16:57,870
Hearing something, I look behind me,

250
00:16:56,700 --> 00:16:59,240
I thought there'd be plenty of chances to come.

251
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:04,290
kyou mo mata mitsukerarenai

252
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:04,290
but it turns out it was just the wind again.

253
00:17:01,370 --> 00:17:02,330
But...

254
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:09,590
I will sotto negatte miru

255
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:09,590
I will make a wish,

256
00:17:09,590 --> 00:17:21,680
anata ni todoke kono basho de atashi wa matteiru

257
00:17:09,590 --> 00:17:21,680
that you'll realize that I am here, waiting for you.

258
00:17:11,170 --> 00:17:14,260
We can never go back.

259
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:17,220
Things have changed since then.

260
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,600
Why does this bother me so much?!

261
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:29,570
School Shop

262
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,360
Over here!

263
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:29,570
Excuse me!

264
00:17:29,570 --> 00:17:33,900
A sweet bean bun, a croquet, and a Danish!

265
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:35,240
That again?

266
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:37,110
Can you even eat all that?

267
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:40,870
I know, right? Doesn't it disgust you?

268
00:17:42,790 --> 00:17:45,660
Wh-Who cares? It's my choice.

269
00:17:46,670 --> 00:17:50,590
The only reason I overeat is to lower my allure...

270
00:17:50,590 --> 00:17:52,500
...but I can't say that out loud.

271
00:17:53,050 --> 00:17:54,880
I'm so despicable!

272
00:17:55,260 --> 00:17:57,300
Excuse me, these please.

273
00:17:57,300 --> 00:17:58,390
I'll take this.

274
00:17:58,390 --> 00:18:00,720
Sure, just a sec.

275
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,220
Sorry, I'm all out of bags.

276
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:06,520
Give me a minute and I'll bring more out.

277
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,980
Oh, don't worry about it.

278
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,440
Are you sure?

279
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,360
That'll be 530 yen.

280
00:18:13,280 --> 00:18:15,360
Good, exact change.

281
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:18,450
Let's see... Where's Chie-chan...

282
00:18:18,450 --> 00:18:20,320
Where do you think you're going?

283
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:24,700
Are you trying to get away without paying?

284
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:27,460
Huh? But I did pay.

285
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:31,460
Don't get smart with me. Those aren't in a bag.

286
00:18:30,630 --> 00:18:32,000
Huh? Futaba?

287
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:33,670
That's because...

288
00:18:33,670 --> 00:18:36,630
Don't give me that. I see you students do this left and right.

289
00:18:36,630 --> 00:18:38,090
No, I...

290
00:18:38,090 --> 00:18:39,760
Futaba?

291
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,640
Asumi, Chie-chan.

292
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:45,970
What do you think you're doing, Futaba? Are you crazy?

293
00:18:45,970 --> 00:18:46,310
Huh?

294
00:18:46,310 --> 00:18:48,890
You gotta pay like everyone else.

295
00:18:48,890 --> 00:18:50,850
I'm telling you, I did!

296
00:18:50,850 --> 00:18:53,440
Pay now and I won't have to tell the teachers about this.

297
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,030
If you'd just listen...

298
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:57,690
She already paid.

299
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:02,780
Excuse me.

300
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:04,160
Yes?

301
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:07,000
She already paid, right?

302
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,210
Yeah, she's good to go.

303
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:13,670
Really? You should've said something sooner.

304
00:19:13,670 --> 00:19:17,010
Whatever... you can go now.

305
00:19:17,010 --> 00:19:19,510
Y-You...

306
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:22,340
Hey, where do you think you're going?

307
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:24,430
Apologize, old hag.

308
00:19:24,430 --> 00:19:26,220
"Hag"?

309
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:29,940
You messed up. You apologize.

310
00:19:31,560 --> 00:19:33,400
I'm so sorry.

311
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:36,900
Uh, yeah... sure.

312
00:19:45,700 --> 00:19:47,660
Hey! Futaba?

313
00:19:49,410 --> 00:19:51,460
Tanaka-kun, wait up!

314
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:56,460
What?

315
00:19:57,840 --> 00:20:00,340
Th-Thank you.

316
00:20:01,130 --> 00:20:03,550
You really helped me out there.

317
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,600
Whatever.

318
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:08,600
She's the one who's got a few screws loose.

319
00:20:08,600 --> 00:20:11,730
Yeah. I was about to snap.

320
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:18,400
But I felt better after you stood up for me.

321
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,820
That's all it took to make you feel better?

322
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:24,780
You're so shallow.

323
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:29,870
And it's because you're like that
that your friendships are shallow.

324
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,960
It's like you're all just pretending to be friends.

325
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:37,920
It's pointless.

326
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:45,430
It might look pointless to you,

327
00:20:46,430 --> 00:20:49,810
but it's all very important to me!

328
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:52,730
What? Just drop it.

329
00:20:52,730 --> 00:20:54,310
I couldn't really care less.

330
00:20:54,310 --> 00:20:56,190
It's your business.

331
00:20:58,060 --> 00:21:02,030
First he saves me, and then brushes me off.

332
00:21:02,030 --> 00:21:03,700
I just don't get him.

333
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:09,620
Is he really the Tanaka-kun I once knew?

334
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,370
Oh, and also...

335
00:21:16,210 --> 00:21:18,920
My name's Mabuchi.

336
00:21:24,930 --> 00:21:27,890
Tanaka Kou is long gone.

337
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:41,440
Just as I've changed, the Tanaka-kun from my memories...

338
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:43,820
...no longer exists.

339
00:21:47,030 --> 00:21:48,620
I can't go back...

340
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:52,740
...to those days.

